# Flutter/Dart Essential Rules

## Architecture

- **Layered architecture**: UI Layer (Views + ViewModel/Cubit/Provider) → Data Layer (Repositories + Services)
- **Feature-first organization**: Group all files for a feature together (e.g., `auth/` contains `auth_viewmodel.dart`, `login_screen.dart`)
- **Unidirectional data flow**: State flows down (Data → UI), events flow up (UI → Data)
- **Repository = Single Source of Truth**: Only repositories mutate data; all other classes read from them
- **Services hold no state**: They only wrap API endpoints

## Naming Conventions

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Classes, enums, typedefs | `UpperCamelCase` | `MyWidget`, `UserState` |
| Files, packages | `lowercase_with_underscores` | `user_profile.dart` |
| Variables, functions | `lowerCamelCase` | `userName`, `fetchData()` |

## Style

- Use `dart format .` — don't manually format
- Prefer `final` over `var`; use `const` for compile-time constants
- Use curly braces for all flow control statements
- Keep lines 80 characters or fewer
- Prefer relative import paths within a package

## Types

- Type annotate variables without initializers
- Annotate return types and parameter types on function declarations
- Use `Future<void>` for async members that don't produce values

## Common Flutter Errors

| Error | Fix |
|-------|-----|
| RenderFlex overflowed | Wrap child in `Expanded` or `Flexible` |
| Vertical viewport unbounded height | Wrap `ListView` in `Expanded` inside `Column` |
| InputDecorator unbounded width | Wrap `TextField` in `Expanded` or `SizedBox` |
| setState during build | Use `addPostFrameCallback` in `initState` |
| RenderBox not laid out | Add size constraints with `SizedBox` or `Expanded` |

## Widgets

- Use `StatelessWidget` when possible
- Keep `build` methods simple and focused
- Extract reusable widgets into separate components
- Use `const` constructors when possible

## State Management

- Keep state as local as possible
- Avoid unnecessary `StatefulWidget`s
- Business logic belongs in ViewModel/Cubit/Provider, NOT in widgets

## Testing

- Every test should be able to fail if real code is broken
- Use `group()` named after the class under test
- Name tests with "should": `test('should return null when not found', () {...})`

## Documentation

- Use `///` doc comments for public APIs
- Start with a single-sentence summary
- Use `[identifier]` to reference in-scope identifiers

